SUMMARY:Deadline: European Cultural Foundation: Artistic Research Fellowshi
 p (ECF Historical Archives)
DESCRIPTION:The European Cultural Foundation invites artists to research it
 s historical archives\, held at the Historical Archives of the European Un
 ion in Florence\, through a new Artistic Research Fellowship with a EUR 10
 \,000 grant covering travel\, accommodation\, and living costs\; the artis
 tic output is delivered within two years. A strong fit for archive-driven\
 , research-based\, and critical data practices. Deadline 30 September 2026
 \, 17:00 CET. ELIGIBILITY: professional creatives in visual arts\, perform
 ing arts\, film and audiovisual practices\, podcasting and audio storytell
 ing\, documentary\, journalism or literary practices\, who can demonstrate
  a research-based practice and a clear dissemination strategy. Application
 s and all supporting documentation must be in English\, submitted via the 
 online form. Fellows work at the HAEU inside the scholarly community of th
 e European University Institute\, with the archives housed at Villa Salvia
 ti. A parallel Academic Research Fellowship of EUR 5\,000\, for PhD and po
 stdoctoral researchers\, early-career researchers within ten years of thei
 r master's or doctorate\, and independent scholars\, is listed separately 
 on the desk and shares this deadline.\n\nOrganisation: European Cultural F
 oundation\nLocation: Archives held at the Historical Archives of the Europ
 ean Union\, Florence\, Italy. Open to artists able to work with the archiv
 es.\nAward: EUR 10\,000 artistic-research grant covering travel\, accommod
 ation\, and living costs\; output delivered within 2 years. No application
  fee.\nDuration: Research fellowship in the ECF historical archives\; outp
 ut within two years.\n\nMore: https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/new
 -fellowship-programme-to-research-the-ecf-historical-archives/?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
